UPDATE companies SET description='Methode Electronics was founded in 1946 by William J. McGinley on the south side of Chicago, Illinois. The company''s name derived from an anagram of "good manufacturing method, electrode and cathode of a vacuum tube." McGinley, a World War II veteran, started the business with a focus on innovation and cutting-edge technology to engineer solutions for customers.

Today headquartered in Southfield, Michigan, Methode Electronics (NYSE: MEI) operates as a global manufacturer of custom-engineered mechatronic products. The company employs approximately 6,500 people across sales, engineering, and manufacturing locations in North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia. Its vertically integrated manufacturing capabilities span assembly, decorating, electronics, metalworking, plastics, and testing, including processes such as injection molding, stamping, PCB assembly, in-mold decorating, and automated optical inspection. The business is organized into three segments—Automotive, Industrial, and Interface—each delivering highly integrated solutions for user interface, LED lighting, power distribution, and sensor applications.

Methode serves original equipment manufacturers across transportation, industrial, and consumer markets. Its automotive segment supplies user-interface, lighting, sensor, and chassis/powertrain solutions to automotive, commercial vehicle, bus, rail, and off-road OEMs. The Industrial segment, through brands such as Grakon, Nordic Lights, Power Solutions Group, and Hetronic, addresses markets including mining, material handling, agriculture, construction, military/aerospace, data centers, energy storage, robotics, and renewable energy. The Interface segment, via TouchSensor and Methode Sensor Technologies, provides touch, display, and sensor solutions for appliances, vending machines, medical equipment, fitness equipment, and e-mobility applications.

The company states its differentiation lies in proprietary and differentiated technology, expertise across multiple applications, highly vertically integrated manufacturing, quality and reliability, and responsiveness to global OEM customer needs. Founder William McGinley''s original vision was to engineer and manufacture solutions that help customers grow their own businesses through innovation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Assembly (lean cells, fully/semi-automated, mistake proofing, variable controlled fastening)", "Clean room assembly (Class 10,000, Class 1,000)", "Laser marking", "UV coating (manual & automated)", "Robotic part placement", "Adhesive dispensing", "Automated paint lines", "In-mold decorating (IMD)", "In-mold labeling (IML)", "Digital printing", "Pad printing", "Precision laser etching", "Hot stamping", "Sputtering (metalization)", "Powder coating", "PCB assembly / processing", "Surface mount technology (SMT) lines", "Wave & selective soldering", "Touch screen optical bonding", "Conformal coating", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "Stamping", "In-house plating", "CNC machining", "Water-jet cutting", "Injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over-molding", "Two-shot molding", "Liquid silicone rubber molding", "Laser welding", "Ultrasonic welding", "End-of-line functional testing (ELOT)", "Environmental testing (thermal shock, vibration, salt spray)", "EMC/EMI testing", "Pressure leak testing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Commercial Vehicle", "Bus/Coach", "Rail", "Sport/Recreation", "Motorcycles", "Off-Road", "Industrial Equipment", "Mining", "Material Handling", "Agriculture", "Forestry", "Construction", "Electric Vehicles", "Military/Aerospace", "Data Center/Storage", "Energy Storage", "Robotics", "Renewable Energy", "Power Conversion", "Industrial Mobile Equipment", "Cranes", "Drones", "Locomotive/Railway", "Marine", "Appliance", "Vending Machines", "Commercial Appliance", "Fitness Equipment", "Medical Equipment", "E-Mobility"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Surface Mount lines (SMT)", "Wave & selective soldering equipment", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) systems", "Environment Chambers", "Thermal Shock Chambers", "Vibration test systems", "EMI/RFI chamber", "Isolated Sound chamber"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary and differentiated technology", "Expertise across multiple applications", "Highly vertically integrated manufacturing", "Quality and reliability", "Responsiveness to global OEM customer needs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1946 by William J. McGinley in Chicago, Illinois -> db (description)", "Headquartered in Southfield, Michigan -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "Employee count 6,500 -> db (employee_count)", "NYSE listed (MEI) -> page /", "Three business segments: Automotive, Industrial, Interface -> page /", "Vertically integrated manufacturing capabilities across assembly, decorating, electronics, metal, plastic, testing -> page /capabilities", "Markets served: automotive, commercial vehicle, bus/coach, rail, off-road, mining, material handling, agriculture, construction, military/aerospace, data center, energy storage, robotics, renewable energy, industrial mobile equipment, cranes, drones, locomotive/railway, marine, appliance, vending machines, medical equipment, e-mobility -> page /", "Differentiators: proprietary technology, multi-application expertise, vertically integrated manufacturing, quality and reliability, responsiveness to global OEM needs -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "design, engineer, and produce mechatronic products for OEMs", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "6500", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='methode-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company operates 30 injection molding machines ranging from 15 to 720 tons, offering two-shot molding, insert molding, in-mold labeling, and prototyping. An in-house tool room and maintenance department support 650 unique active molds, some with up to 12 cavities cycling every 22 seconds. An on-site metrology lab provides real-time dimensional inspection and PPAP/FAI capabilities. Annual output runs between 35 and 50 million parts.

Metro Plastics serves a diverse customer base that includes Moonlight Concepts LLC, O2 Blast, and AM Leonard. The company emphasizes long-term partnerships and provides domestic and offshore tooling options through its network in the MAPP Association.

The company differentiates itself through a relationship-focused approach, an on-time delivery guarantee that refunds 10 percent of the order if a shipping date is missed, and a commitment to environmental responsibility. Its quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015, and the firm promotes accountability through its Metro Tooling Standard.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Two-shot molding", "Insert molding", "In-mold labeling", "Custom automation", "Custom packaging", "Prototyping", "In-house tooling and maintenance", "Metrology and inspection (PPAP/FAI)", "Domestic and offshore tooling sourcing", "Material selection consulting", "Mold analysis", "Manufacturability advice"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["30 injection molding machines (15-720 ton capacity)", "On-site metrology lab"], "volume": "35-50 million parts annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["On-time delivery guarantee \u2013 10% off if shipping date missed", "In-house tool room and maintenance department", "On-site metrology lab for real-time dimensional feedback", "650 unique active molds managed at one facility", "Domestic and offshore tooling options via MAPP Association"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 -> db", "Headquarters Noblesville, Indiana -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "30 injection molding machines 15-720 tons -> /", "Two-shot molding -> /", "Insert molding -> /", "In-house tool room -> /", "On-site metrology lab -> /quality", "650 unique active molds -> /", "35-50 million parts annually -> /", "On-time delivery guarantee 10% off -> /", "Domestic and offshore tooling -> /", "MAPP Association membership -> /", "Environmentally aware -> /", "In-mold labeling -> /", "Custom automation -> /", "Custom packaging -> /", "Prototyping -> /", "PPAP/FAI -> /quality", "Material selection, mold analysis, manufacturability advice -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_pro