UPDATE companies SET description='MiDAS Foods International operates from its main campus in Oak Park, Michigan, with a second facility in Birmingham, Alabama. The company has been developing dry blends and food solutions for over 40 years. Partners Richard Elias and Gary Freeman lead the business alongside a team of culinary and R&D executives.

The company engineers shelf-stable dry blends — including sauces, gravies, glazes, seasonings, soup mixes, cheese sauces, batter mixes, and dessert bases — that replicate or exceed scratch-made quality. Its combined U.S. R&D and manufacturing footprint exceeds 150,000 square feet, and an affiliate plant in Kashipur, India (Dry Blend Foods) serves more than 20 countries. The culinary team handles custom formulation, clean-label and plant-based ingredient systems, and manufacturing optimization.

MiDAS serves food processors, manufacturers, and casual-dining restaurant chains across the United States. Customers use its blends to replace ready-to-use sauces that are costly to ship and store, reducing SKU count, batching errors, and waste. Regional product lines cover North/Midwest and South/Southeast flavor profiles, from Michigan baked bean seasoning to Nashville hot sauce and Cajun étouffée mixes.

The company emphasizes sustainability: dry blends cut shipping weight, eliminate refrigeration, and lower energy use by three to six times compared with prepared sauces. MiDAS was built to give manufacturers and restaurants a single-source ingredient that delivers consistent flavor, faster prep, and lower total cost.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dry blend manufacturing", "Custom food product development", "Culinary recipe formulation", "Clean-label ingredient systems", "Plant-based ingredient systems", "Manufacturing process optimization", "Food R&D and sensory testing", "Versatile packaging solutions", "Sauce and gravy replication", "Seasoning and spice blending", "Soup and sauce mix production", "Cheese sauce and dairy blend production", "Batter and coating mix production", "Dessert and bakery mix production", "Flavor profiling and matching", "Quality assurance and food safety (FSQA)"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Food processing", "Casual dining restaurants", "Restaurant chains", "Commercial kitchens", "Foodservice"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dry blends cut shipping weight, eliminate refrigeration, and reduce energy use 3\u20136\u00d7 versus prepared sauces", "Blends match or exceed scratch-made flavor, texture, color, and consistency", "Custom formulation with culinary R&D team and clean-label/plant-based ingredient systems", "Single-source ingredient reduces SKU handling, batching mistakes, and waste", "Over 150,000 sq ft of U.S. R&D and manufacturing space across two campuses"], "facts_used": ["Location: Oak Park, Michigan -> db", "Facility size: Over 150,000 sq ft combined R&D & manufacturing space in US -> /", "Affiliate: Dry Blend Foods in Kashipur, India exporting to 20+ countries -> /", "Products: Dry blends including sauces, gravies, glazes, seasonings, soup mixes, cheese sauces, batter mixes, dessert bases -> /", "Customers: Food manufactur