UPDATE companies SET description='Micro Metals, Inc. was founded in 1972 by Kenny Driscoll in Colorado Springs, Colorado, at an elevation of 6,272 feet. The family‑owned and operated company began as a precision sheet‑metal fabrication shop and has remained a single‑source manufacturer of custom metal products for over five decades.

Today the firm operates a 141,000‑square‑foot facility with a secured 208,000‑square‑foot outside storage yard. Its highly automated processes include three laser‑cutting systems, waterjet cutting, robotic and manual press brakes, robotic and manual welding, CNC machining (VMC, HMC, VTC), CNC punching, coil punching, rollforming, blanking, assembly, engineering support, and an in‑house powder‑ and liquid‑coating line that is CARC‑certified. The workforce is notable for its tenure: machinists average 15 years on the shop floor, and the engineering department includes several military veterans.

Micro Metals serves customers in telecommunications, U.S. military, energy, climate‑control, construction, and secure‑storage industries, shipping to local, national, and international clients from its central Rocky Mountain location.

The company emphasizes its “one‑stop” model—quoting, designing, manufacturing, assembling, and shipping under one roof—to control lead times and supply‑chain risk. A culture of continuous improvement, family values, and a commitment to Made‑in‑USA production underpin its reputation for speed, trust, and cost‑efficient manufacturing. Philanthropic efforts have also placed Micro Metals parts in humanitarian building projects on four continents.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001','NADCAP','CARC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automated Laser Cutting", "Waterjet Cutting", "Robotic & Manual Press Brakes", "Robotic & Manual Welding", "Automated Powder & Liquid Coating", "CARC Coating", "Automated Coil Punching & Rollforming", "CNC Machining (VMC, HMC, VTC)", "CNC Punching", "Blanking & Punching", "Assembly & Support", "Engineering", "Surface Finishing"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "U.S. Military", "Energy", "Climate Control", "Construction", "Secure Storage"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["3 automated laser cutting systems", "State-of-the-art robotic press brake", "Automated coil punching and rollformers", "CNC machining centers (VMC, HMC, VTC)", "Robotic welding cells", "Automated powder and liquid coating line", "In-house paint division", "State-of-the-art inspection equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source manufacturing: quote, design, fabricate, assemble, and ship under one roof", "In-house CARC\u2011certified powder and liquid coating eliminates outsourcing", "Three automated laser\u2011cutting systems and robotic press brakes for high\u2011speed precision", "141,000 sq ft facility with 208,000 sq ft secured outside storage", "Experienced workforce with machinists averaging 15 years and veteran\u2011staffed engineering"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Kenny Driscoll -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Headquarters Colorado Springs, Colorado -> /about-us", "141,000 sq ft facility with 208,000 sq ft outside storage -> /about-us", "ISO9001 and NADCAP certifications -> db", "Capabilities: laser cutting, waterjet, press brakes, welding, coating, coil punching, rollforming, CNC machining, assembly, engineering -> /capabilities", "Industries: Telecommunications, U.S. Military, Energy, Climate Control, Construction, Secure Storage -> /", "Single-source manufacturer model -> /", "In-house CARC-certified powder and liquid coating -> /capabilities", "Three automated laser cutting systems -> /", "Robotic press brake -> /", "Machinists average 15 years tenure -> /about-us", "Engineering department staffed with military veterans -> /about-us", "Made in USA since 1972 -> /about-us", "Philanthropic parts for buildings on four continents -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Micro Metals is a highly automated manufacturer of custom metal products & trusted, single source, supplier of precision parts to companies for more than 50 years.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='micro-metals-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Micro-Precision Technologies, Inc. was founded in 1998 in Salem, New Hampshire.

The company focuses on thick film hybrid circuits screened onto ceramic substrates such as alumina, aluminum nitride, and beryllium oxide. Its capabilities include hybrid assembly with manual and automated surface-mount technology, wire bonding (ball and wedge), die attach, and semiconductor repackaging. Work is performed in a Class 10,000 cleanroom, and the firm also offers FR-4 to ceramic conversion services for improved thermal management.

Micro-Precision serves industrial, military, and medical markets, supplying components for harsh environments including extreme heat, high vibration, downhole mining, deep-sea wells, and space applications.

The company differentiates itself through its long-standing MIL-PRF-38534 Class H qualification (since 1998), QML-38534 listing, and DSCC certification, combined with AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 quality systems and ITAR registration. Its ceramic substrates provide inherent thermal management advantages over traditional FR-4 boards.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL-PRF-38534 Class H','QML-38534','DSCC certified','AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thick film circuit screening", "Ceramic substrate fabrication (alumina, aluminum nitride, beryllium oxide)", "Hybrid assembly (manual and automated SMT)", "Wire bonding (ball and wedge)", "Die attach (auto die attach, auto dispense)", "Semiconductor packaging/repackaging", "FR-4 to ceramic conversion", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Consigned or full turnkey assemblies", "Class 10,000 cleanroom assembly", "Encapsulation and optical fluid dispensing"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Military", "Medical"], "materials": ["Alumina", "Aluminum Nitride", "Beryllium Oxide", "FR-4", "Epoxy", "Encapsulant", "Optical fluid"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["MIL-PRF-38534 Class H qualified since 1998", "QML-38534 listed and DSCC certified", "AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "ITAR registered", "Class 10,000 cleanroom for hybrid assembly"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 -> db", "Headquarters Salem, New Hampshire -> db", "MIL-PRF-38534 Class H qualified since 1998 -> page ''/''", "QML-38534 listed -> page ''/''", "DSCC certified -> page ''/''", "AS9100D certified -> page ''/''", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> page ''/''", "ITAR registered -> page ''/''", "Class 10,000 cleanroom -> page ''/''", "Thick film hybrid capabilities -> page ''/''", "Ceramic substrates: alumina, aluminum nitride, beryllium oxide -> page ''/''", "Industries: Industrial, Military, Medical -> db", "Hybrid assembly: SMT, wire bonding, die attach -> page ''/''", "Semiconduct