UPDATE companies SET description='Microfit Autobody Parts Supply operates from Beltsville, Maryland, where it runs an e-commerce platform for auto body parts and mirrors. The company’s founding year, ownership structure, and founder names are not disclosed in public sources.

The business distributes replacement body panels, bumpers, mirrors, and related components for a broad range of passenger cars and commercial trucks. Its website features a year-make-model lookup covering more than 60 brands — from Acura, Chevrolet, and Ford to BMW, Mercedes-Benz, and Volvo — as well as heavy-duty lines such as Freightliner, International, Kenworth, and Peterbilt. Orders are processed through an online cart, and the company publishes a return policy that requires a Return Goods Authorization (RMA), proof of purchase, and accepts parts with intact CAPA seals within 10 days of invoice; parts with broken seals or that have been altered, painted, or damaged are ineligible.

