UPDATE companies SET description='MicroLink Devices was founded in 2000 in Niles, Illinois, a northern suburb of Chicago. The company operates a 30,000-square-foot facility that houses a clean room, device fabrication and test laboratories, and a full suite of metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) tools for high-volume epitaxial growth.

The company designs and manufactures III-V epitaxial materials for wireless communications, including cellular phones, and produces high-efficiency single- and multi-junction gallium arsenide (GaAs) solar cells and sheets for unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), spacecraft, and terrestrial collectors. Its proprietary epitaxial lift-off (ELO) process separates the solar cell structure from the growth substrate, yielding lightweight, flexible cells while allowing the substrate to be reused multiple times. MicroLink owns all equipment needed for growth, fabrication, and testing of epitaxial materials and solar devices.

Since 2003 it has been a prime federal contractor on more than thirty programs developing solar cells, transistors, and lasers. Its customer base includes government agencies and commercial firms seeking custom epitaxial materials, solar sheets for UAVs and satellites, and contract research and development support.

The company emphasizes quality and technical depth: it is ISO 9001 certified, employs staff recognized as experts in GaAs- and InP-based device growth and processing, and supports customers through both development and production phases to improve yield and performance. The ELO technology, developed through its federal R&D programs, is cited as a key differentiator that reduces cost and enables flexible, high-specific-power solar solutions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and manufacture of III-V epitaxial materials", "Design and manufacture of GaAs solar cells and solar sheets", "Epitaxial lift-off (ELO) process", "Metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD)", "Device fabrication and testing", "Contract research and development", "Engineering services", "Quality control and assurance"], "industries": ["Aerospace (UAVs, spacecraft)", "Defense / federal government", "Renewable energy (terrestrial solar collectors)", "Wireless communications (cellular phones)"], "materials": ["Gallium Arsenide (GaAs)", "Indium Phosphide (InP)", "III-V compound semiconductors"], "equipment": ["Metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) tools", "Clean room", "Device fabrication and test laboratory"], "volume": "High volume production capable", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary epitaxial lift-off (ELO) process enabling lightweight, flexible solar cells with substrate reuse", "MOCVD tools for high-volume III-V epitaxial growth", "ISO 9001 certified quality management", "Prime federal contractor on 30+ programs since 2003", "In-house clean room and device fabrication/test laboratories"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Niles, Illinois -> /about-us", "30,000 sq ft facility with clean room and device fabrication/test lab -> /about-us", "Owns MOCVD tools for high volume production -> /about-us", "Designs and manufactures III-V epitaxial material for cellular phones and wireless devices -> /about-us", "Designs and manufactures GaAs solar cells and sheets for UAVs, spacecraft, terrestrial collectors -> /about-us", "Proprietary epitaxial lift-off (ELO) technology -> /about-us", "ISO 9001 certified -> /about-us", "Prime federal contractor on 30+ programs since 2003 -> /about-us", "Contract R&D services -> /about-us", "Expert staff in GaAs and InP device growth and processing -> /about-us", "Engineering services offered -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MicroLink Devices'' core business is the design and manufacture of III-V epitaxial material used in cellular phones and other wireless devices, and the design and manufacture of solar cells and solar sheets for a variety of applications, including unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), spacecraft, and terrestrial collectors.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='microlink-devices-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Micross Components - TX, LLC operates from Round Rock, Texas. The company''s expertise dates to 1984 when it pioneered robotic hot solder dip (RHSD) for high-reliability microelectronics.

The facility provides a broad suite of component modification and qualification services. Core processes include BGA reballing, robotic hot solder dip, lead attach, column grid array (CGA) attachment, and lead trim/form and reconditioning. Additional capabilities span printed circuit board assembly, rework, and repair, as well as component harvesting from existing assemblies. Support services encompass tape-and-reel packaging, 3D scanning, bake-and-package cycles, marking, labeling, and kitting. The company also performs component qualification testing such as fine and gross leak detection, acoustic microscopy, X-ray inspection, and X-ray fluorescence analysis.

Customers come from space, defense, aerospace, medical, and communications sectors, along with other high-reliability markets. The company positions itself as a single-source provider for component-level services, offering turnkey programs and supplier-managed inventory (SMI) options.

