UPDATE companies SET description='The pair began by refurbishing used furniture in a garage, turning a passion for furniture into a business. Within a year they expanded to sourcing new furniture and opened their first retail location in Moorhead, followed by a second store in Excelsior.

The company operates two Minnesota showrooms — in Moorhead and Excelsior — selling a range of new and like‑new home furnishings including sectionals, sofas, dining sets, accent chairs, bedroom pieces and outdoor furniture. They source much of their inventory through a direct partnership with Ashley Furniture. In addition to retail sales, Minnesofa offers a white‑glove delivery service that covers in‑home setup and trash removal across the Twin Cities metro area.

Minnesofa serves residential customers throughout the Twin Cities region, providing living‑room, dining‑room and bedroom furniture for homeowners and renters. The company’s focus on sectionals and quick turnaround appeals to buyers who need furniture delivered and assembled on a tight schedule.

The founders emphasize speed and personal service as their differentiators: most items can be delivered within a week, and customers work directly with the owners rather than a sales staff. The white‑glove delivery model, which includes setup and debris removal, is designed to remove the hassle of moving large pieces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail furniture sales", "White glove delivery and installation", "Furniture refurbishment", "In-home setup and trash removal"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Within a week for most products", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Delivery within a week for most products", "White glove delivery with in-home setup and trash removal", "Direct owner-to-customer service", "Locally owned and operated in Excelsior and Moorhead, MN"], "facts_used": ["Founded May 2022 by Max Bjorklund and Luke Schultz -> /", "Started refurbishing used furniture in a garage -> /", "Opened retail locations in Moorhead and Excelsior, MN -> /", "Direct partnership with Ashley Furniture -> /", "White glove delivery service with in-home setup and trash removal -> /", "Delivery within a week for most products -> /", "Locally owned and operated by founders -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "We are locally owned and operated in Excelsior & Moorhead, MN, offering a variety of like-new and brand-new products", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='minnesofa-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Minnesota Medical Technologies is headquartered in Stewartville, Minnesota, just outside Rochester. The company was founded by Philip J. Conway, Sarah L. Grinde, and Lonnie M. Boe, who brought decades of experience in silicone technology and medical device development from prior ventures including Rochester Medical Corporation and Arcon Corp. The team set out to create a better solution for fecal incontinence after recognizing that existing products failed to adequately prevent leakage or restore patients'' confidence.

The company develops, manufactures, and sells continence care products, most notably the StaySure® device—a discreet, silicone-based system designed to prevent accidental bowel leakage rather than merely contain or absorb it. Minnesota Medical Technologies designs and builds its own highly specialized, high-volume production systems, leveraging over 30 years of silicone expertise to control quality from concept through manufacturing.

The company serves the medical device and healthcare industries, focusing on fecal incontinence management. Its products are developed in collaboration with gastroenterologists and are intended for individuals living with fecal incontinence, as well as clinicians seeking advanced treatment options. The team includes veterans of Rochester Medical Corporation, C.R. Bard, and Polaris Industries, bringing regulatory, quality, and commercial experience across Class I, II, and III medical devices.

Minnesota Medical Technologies was started because the founders believed current fecal incontinence products were not good enough—often failing to prevent leakage, control odor, or provide ease of use. Their mission is to deliver products of unmatched performance, comfort, and quality worldwide, restoring dignity and freedom to patients through innovative engineering and clinical insight.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device development", "Silicone molding and technology", "Product design and engineering", "High-volume production system design and manufacturing", "Quality system design and implementation (FDA)", "Regulatory affairs management", "Research and development", "Global product deployment and commercialization", "Commercial sales strategy execution"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Healthcare", "Continence care", "Fecal incontinence management"], "materials": ["Silicone"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["StaySure\u00ae prevents accidental leakage rather than containing or absorbing it", "Developed in collaboration with leading gastroenterologists", "Over 30 years of silicone technology and medical device innovation", "In-house design and construction of high-volume production systems", "Team with deep FDA regulatory and quality experience across Class I\u2013III devices"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Stewartville, MN -> /about-us", "Mission: develop, make, sell continence care products -> /about-us, /", "Product: StaySure\u00ae device for fecal incontinence -> /", "Team has 30+ years silicone technology experience -> /about-us", "Founders: Philip J Conway, Sarah L Grinde, Lonnie M Boe -> /about-us", "David A Jones CEO and President -> /about-us", "Design and build own high-volume production systems -> /about-us", "Developed with world''s top gastroenterologists -> /", "Prevent accidental leakage, not contain or absorb -> /", "Robert M Anglin VP Quality and Regu