UPDATE companies SET description='Mitchell Furniture Systems traces its roots to Milwaukee, Wisconsin, where William Mitchell founded the company in 1896 to produce dairy-farm equipment such as automatic stalls, pens, and stanchions. Over the next decades the firm expanded its metal-fabricating expertise into park and playground steel products sold nationwide.

Today Mitchell operates plants in Fredonia and Milwaukee, where seasoned fabricators and assemblers combine time-honored metalworking with robotic welding to build the company''s full line of tables and seating. The product range includes wall-mounted table-and-bench systems (a category Mitchell pioneered in the early 1950s), mobile PorTables with integrated seating, Fold-N-Roll folding tables, 3-in-1 ConverTables that convert cafeteria space to theater or lecture configurations, Saturna adjustable-height and Fold-O-Leg folding tables, and choral risers. Steel frames paired with wood tops remain the core construction method, and the company also offers a top-replacement service for both its own tables and competitors'' units.

Primary customers are K–12 school districts, municipalities, churches, and commercial offices that need durable cafeteria, classroom, fellowship-hall, conference-room, and lecture-hall furniture. Mitchell''s risers have served educational and municipal facilities since the late 1940s, and many early installations remain in service.

The company emphasizes "Made in America By Mitchell" as its differentiator, citing domestic production, robotic welding precision, and a design philosophy aimed at decades-long product life. Immediate delivery is advertised for stocked items.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "Robotic welding", "Wall-mounted table and bench system manufacturing", "Mobile table manufacturing (PorTables)", "Folding table manufacturing (Fold-N-Roll, Saturna Adjustable Height, Fold-O-Leg)", "Convertible table manufacturing (ConverTables)", "Riser and stand manufacturing", "Table top replacement service"], "industries": ["Education (K-12 schools)", "Municipal government", "Religious institutions (churches)", "Commercial offices", "Hospitality (fellowship halls, lunch rooms)", "Performing arts (theaters, lecture halls)"], "materials": ["Steel", "Wood (table tops)"], "equipment": ["Robotic welding systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Available for immediate delivery on stocked items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Domestic manufacturing in Fredonia and Milwaukee, Wisconsin", "Robotic welding integrated with traditional metal fabrication", "Table-top replacement service for Mitchell and competitor products", "Wall-mounted table/bench systems since the early 1950s", "Risers and stands with documented service life since the 1940s"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1896 in Milwaukee by William Mitchell -> /about-us", "Plants in Fredonia and Milwaukee, Wisconsin -> /about-us", "Metal fabrication with robotic welding -> /about-us", "Wall-mounted table/bench systems since early 1950s -> /, /about-us", "Product lines: PorTables, Fold-N-Roll, ConverTables, Saturna, Fold-O-Leg, risers -> /", "Steel frames with wood tops -> /about-us", "Top replacement service for Mitchell and competitor tables -> /", "Serves K-12 schools, municipalities, churches, offices -> /", "Risers since late 1940s, many still in use -> /", "\"Made in America By Mitchell\" positioning