UPDATE companies SET description='Mitsubishi Electric US, Inc., Industrial Automation operates from a facility in Vernon Hills, Illinois, serving as the Americas hub for the Japanese conglomerate''s factory automation business. The parent company, Mitsubishi Electric Corporation, marked its 100th anniversary in February 2021, with the factory automation division representing a substantial portion of that legacy. The U.S. division was established to consolidate sales, marketing, service, engineering, and manufacturing resources under one roof.

The division designs and manufactures a broad portfolio of industrial automation equipment, including programmable logic controllers (MELSEC iQ-R, iQ-F, Q, L, and F series), human-machine interfaces (GOT3000 series), variable frequency drives (FREQROL FR-D800 series), AC servo systems (MELSERVO), industrial robots (MELFA), collaborative robots (ASSISTA), computerized numerical controllers, laser processing machines, and electrical discharge machines. The Vernon Hills campus integrates manufacturing, engineering, training, customer service, repair, sales, and warehousing functions, enabling end-to-end support for automation deployments.

Customers span mining, water and wastewater treatment, automotive, and education sectors. Documented projects include a comprehensive automation solution for mining safety and material handling with DICISA, a municipal lift station pump upgrade for energy efficiency with Bertelkamp Automation, robotic machine tending for e-motor production at Renault Group, and hands-on automation technology programs at Kettering University. The company also supports a network of Diamond Partner distributors, solutions providers, and OEMs, as well as system integrators through its Solutions Partner program.

The division''s stated mission is to support the industrial automation needs of customers in the Americas through combined resources and a culture of continuous improvement (Kaizen). Mitsubishi Electric ranks among the top five global filers of international patent applications, and the company emphasizes product security through dedicated vulnerability management initiatives. Quality management systems underpin its commitment to meeting or exceeding customer expectations, while rapid repair turnaround using custom parts and on-site training aim to minimize downtime.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial automation product manufacturing", "Engineering and application support", "Customer training (on-site and facility-based)", "Repair and maintenance services", "Technical support and troubleshooting", "Warehousing and distribution", "Product security and vulnerability management", "Quality management system", "Custom parts manufacturing for repair", "Automation system integration support", "Diamond Partner distributor/solutions/OEM network management", "Solutions Partner system integrator program", "e-F@ctory IoT-based smart factory solutions", "FA Integrated Selection Tool for product configuration", "Product software and freeware provision", "Knowledge base and documentation library"], "industries": ["Mining", "Water and wastewater treatment", "Automotive", "Education", "General industrial automation", "Municipal infrastructure"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["MELSEC iQ-R Series PLCs", "MELSEC iQ-F Series PLCs", "MELSEC-Q Series PLCs", "MELSEC-L Series PLCs", "MELSEC-F Series PLCs", "GOT3000 Series HMIs", "FREQROL FR-D800 Series VFDs", "MELSERVO AC Servo Systems", "MELFA Industrial Robots", "ASSISTA Collaborative Robots", "Computerized Numerical Controllers (CNCs)", "Laser Processing Machines", "Electrical Discharge Machines (EDM)", "Low-voltage Circuit Breakers", "Contactors and Motor Starters", "Power Management Meters"], "vol