UPDATE companies SET description='Monterey Mills operates from Janesville, Wisconsin. The company traces its current ownership to February 1995, when Dan Sinykin purchased the former Roller Fabrics after spending seven months working there without pay to evaluate the business. Sinykin, a former Procter & Gamble sales executive and founder of the Tailor’s Touch retail chain, assembled a management team, consolidated multiple plants, and expanded the product line into automotive, equestrian, apparel, hospital, and pet markets.

The mill specializes in sliver knitting — also called high-pile knitting — a labor‑intensive process that locks individual acrylic fibers into a lightweight knit backing. The technique yields fabrics that are warmer than fleece, odor‑ and mildew‑resistant, and machine washable. An in‑house R&D team controls fiber and yarn selection, pile height, density, tensile strength, width, color, and stitch count to develop performance fabrics for diverse applications. The company also produces blankets, bedding, and medical and pet products, all manufactured in the United States.

Customers span medical, pet, automotive, equestrian, apparel, and hospital sectors, as well as the blanket and bedding market. The firm’s technical capabilities allow it to tailor fabric specifications for OEMs and brand owners seeking custom performance textiles.

Monterey Mills positions itself as one of the few remaining U.S. practitioners of sliver knitting, a craft many competitors abandoned due to its complexity. The company emphasizes continuous improvement, domestic production, and sustainability — sourcing recycled raw materials, repurposing all production waste, and treating and reusing wastewater.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sliver knitting", "High-pile knitting", "In-house research and development", "Fiber and yarn selection", "Pile height control", "Density control", "Tensile strength control", "Width control", "Color control", "Stitch count control", "Quality control", "Sustainability practices (recycled raw materials, waste repurposing, wastewater treatment)"], "industries": ["Medical", "Pet Products", "Automotive", "Equestrian", "Apparel", "Hospital", "Blankets & Bedding"], "materials": ["Acrylic fibers", "Recycled raw materials", "Colorfast dyes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of only a few U.S. manufacturers still using sliver knitting", "In-house R&D team controlling fiber/yarn selection, pile height, density, tensile strength, width, color, and stitch count", "All production waste repurposed; wastewater treated and reused", "Made in USA manufacturing", "Continuous improvement targeting world\u2011premier sliver knitter status"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Janesville, Wisconsin -> db", "Founded/purchased in February 1995 -> /", "Owner Dan Sinykin, former Procter & Gamble executive and Tailor''s Touch founder -> /", "Sliver knitting (high-pile knitting) process -> /", "Products: Medical & Pet Products, Blankets & Bedding Products, Made In USA Products -> db", "Industries served: Medical, Pet, Automotive, Equestrian, Apparel, Hospital, Blankets & Bedding -> /", "In-house R&D team controlling fiber/yarn selection, pile height, density, tensile strength, width, color, stitch count -> /", "Sustainability: recycled raw materials, waste repurposing, wastewater treatment and reuse -> /", "Made in USA manufacturing -> /", "Consolidated multiple manufacturing facilities -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Monterey Mills is one of only a few manufacturers remaining that uses this superior technique of producing fabric", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='monterey-mills' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Montrose Molders operates from Piscataway, New Jersey, where it was founded in 1966 by William Bruce Wilson. The company began as a 22-person tool shop producing tight-tolerance molds for the plastics industry. In 1972, the addition of its first injection molding press set the direction for future growth. Today, the business remains family-owned, led by the Wilson family, now in its fourth generation of plastics manufacturing.

The firm functions as a vertically integrated custom plastics manufacturer. Its facility houses 51 injection molding machines ranging from 40 to 1,000 tons of clamp force, two extrusion lines with co-extrusion capability, and an on-site tool and die shop that builds both aluminum and steel molds. A 25,000-square-foot assembly area runs up to five lines simultaneously, supporting decoration, assembly, and packaging. Engineering services include mold flow simulation via Solidworks Plastics and industrial design to translate concepts into 3D models.

Montrose serves a range of sectors including automotive, aerospace, medical devices, electronics, lighting, safety, battery, retail, and consumer goods. Customers engage the company for contract injection molding, extrusion, tooling, and full assembly programs, relying on its one-stop-shop model from design through finished product shipment.

The company emphasizes its family legacy and a culture of quality, consistency, and value. Each client is assigned a dedicated project manager to oversee complex projects from concept to delivery. Montrose highlights its ISO 9001:2015 certification and a focus on shortening lead times and reducing costs as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (40\u20131,000 ton)", "Extrusion with co-extrusion", "Tool and die production", "Assembly and packaging", "Mold flow simulation (Solidworks Plastics)", "Industrial design and engineering", "Part decoration"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aerospace", "Medical devices", "Electronics", "Lighting", "Safety", "Battery", "Retail", "Consumer goods"], "materials": ["Engineering-grade plastics", "Commodity plastics"], "equipment": ["51 injection molding machines (40\u20131,000 ton clamp force)", "Two extrusion lines with co-extrusion capability", "Solidworks Plastics Simulation software"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated manufacturing from part design to finished assembly", "On-site tool and die production with latest engineering technology", "Dedicated project manager assigned to every customer", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Family-owned with four generations of plastics manufacturing experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1966 -> /about (Our Story) and db", "Headquarters Piscataway, New Jersey -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about (Committed to Excellence) and db (certifications)", "51 injection molding machines 40-1000 ton -> /services (Injection Molding)", "Two extrusion lines with co-extrusion -> /services (Extrusion)", "On-site tool and die shop -> /about (What We Do) and /services (Tool & Die Production)", "Assembly space 25,000 ft\u00b2, 5 lines -> /services (Assembly)", "Mold flow simulation using Solidworks Plastics -> /services (Mold Flow)", "Industrial design services -> /services (Industrial Design)", "Family-owned, Wilson family, four generations -> /about (A Family Legacy)", "Industries served: Retail, Battery, Automotive, Lighting, Safety, Aerospace, Electronics, Medical devices, Consumer goods -> /about (Your Go-To for...)", "Dedicated project manager per customer -> / (Project management)", "Vertically integrated manufacturer -> /about (Our Story)", "Started as 22-person tool shop in 1966 -> /about (Our Story)", "First injection molding press 1972 -> /about (Our Story)", "Founder William Bruce Wilson -> /about (Founder William Bruce Wilson hard at work)", "Part decoration, assembly, packing -> / (What We Do) and /about (What We Do)", "One-stop solution for plastics manufacturing -> /about (Montrose truly offers a one-stop solution)", "Commitment to quality, consistency, value -> /about (Committed to Excellence)", "Fast lead times -> / (Montrose has delivered its customers superior service, unmatched quality, and fast lead times)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Montrose Molders Corp. is a custom plastics manufacturer with 51 injection molding machines and presses that range in size from 40 tons to 1,000 tons of clamp force.", "founded_year": "1966", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='montrose-molders' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='More Than A Bakery operates from Versailles, Kentucky, as part of a family-owned contract manufacturing group tracing its roots to 1855 in Richmond, Indiana.

The company produces cookies, crackers, and custom crumb and coating products for food service suppliers. Its capabilities include custom crumb and coating formulation, dessert crumb and coating production, R&D and product development, and product scale-up services. Finished goods can be packaged in bag-in-a-box, kraft bags, or super sacks.

