UPDATE companies SET description='Moriden America, Inc. was established in 1988 as a U.S. subsidiary of Japan''s Moriden Company LTD, which has over 80 years of experience in automotive, transportation, and furniture industries. Today it is headquartered in Carmel, Indiana, led by Vice President Minoru Sudo.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures automotive interior components across three main product lines: seating materials, interior trim, and cargo systems. Its capabilities include compression molding of coated carpets with soft trim and hardware, and an integrated production line for HS-RIM (high-strength reaction injection molding) cargo floor boards that minimize weight and maximize strength. Product offerings range from trunk trim parts and shift boots to upholstery, mat floors, rear seat backs, and tonneau covers.

Moriden America serves the automotive industry, supplying decorative and functional interior trim components to vehicle manufacturers and tier suppliers. Its seating materials, interior trim, and cargo systems are designed to meet the quality, safety, and delivery requirements of automotive programs.

The company emphasizes continuous improvement in safety, quality, cost, delivery, and management, tailoring processes to each project as a key differentiator. It also highlights end-to-end service from development proposal through design, production, quality control, logistics, and sales.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Compression molding", "HS-RIM (high-strength reaction injection molding)", "Simulation-based upholstery design", "Integrated production line for cargo floor boards", "Design planning and development", "Quality control", "Logistics and sales support"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": ["Coated carpets", "Soft trim materials", "Hardware", "HS-RIM composite", "Upholstery fabrics"], "equipment": ["HS-RIM integrated production line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated HS-RIM production line for lightweight, high-strength cargo floor boards", "Flexible production processes enabling quick response to customer needs", "Simulation-driven upholstery design for comfort optimization", "Commitment to continuous improvement across safety, quality, cost, delivery, and management", "End-to-end service from development proposal through logistics and sales"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 -> /about", "Began operations in Detroit, Michigan, 1989 -> /about", "Expanded to Indianapolis 1990 -> /about", "Consolidated operations in Indianapolis 1993 -> /about", "Headquarters in Carmel, Indiana -> /about, /", "Subsidiary of Moriden Company LTD Japan -> /about", "ISO 9001 certification -> /about", "Capabilities: compression molding -> db", "Product lines: seating materials, interior trim, cargo systems -> /about", "HS-RIM integrated production line -> /", "Automotive industry focus -> /, /about", "Representative Minoru Sudo, Vice President -> /about", "Flexible production processes -> /", "Simulation technology for upholstery -> /", "Continuous improvement in safety, quality, cost, del