UPDATE companies SET description='Mountain Pacific Machinery, Inc., doing business as MountPac, operates from Lake Oswego, Oregon. The company has represented manufacturers of food processing, packaging, and product inspection equipment for over fifty years, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership details and founder names are not stated in available sources.

MountPac does not manufacture equipment itself; rather, it specifies, supplies, and integrates machinery from multiple manufacturers. Its scope covers design consultation, installation, and ongoing support for processing, sorting, and packaging lines. The firm maintains a sales team across Oregon, Washington, Montana, Idaho, Utah, Colorado, and Wyoming, along with a dedicated aftermarket parts and field service group.

The company serves food processors handling fresh, frozen, and dry products — including fruits, vegetables, pulses, seeds, and dehydrated items. Applications range from sizing and grading to de-clumping, washing, peeling, optical sorting, conveying, and pouch filling and sealing. Customers also rely on MountPac for inspection systems that remove defects and foreign material.

MountPac emphasizes a design-through-support model aimed at maximizing line efficiency, leveraging long-standing relationships with equipment builders to deliver integrated automation solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Equipment specification and selection", "Systems integration", "Installation and commissioning", "Aftermarket parts supply", "Field service and repair", "Process design consulting", "Product sizing and grading", "De-clumping and singulating", "Washing, scrubbing, and peeling", "Optical sorting (color, shape, defect detection)", "Product conveying and elevating", "Pre-made pouch filling and sealing", "Foreign material inspection"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Food packaging", "Product inspection", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Frozen food processing", "Dry food processing", "Pulse and seed processing", "Dehydrated food processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Product Sizing & Grading Solutions", "De-Clumpers / Product Singulators / Breakers", "Washing, scrubbing, and product peeling machines", "Ingenuity and Raynbow sensor-based whole product sorters", "Series color and shape sorters for dry products", "Series color and shape sorters for wet and frozen products", "Product Lifting Conveyor (S and C configurations)", "Pre-made pouch filling and sealing machines", "Defect and foreign material removal sorters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design through install and support for processing, sorting, and packaging lines", "Over fifty years representing manufacturers of food processing equipment", "Dedicated aftermarket parts and field service teams", "Multi-state sales coverage across the Western U.S."], "facts_used": ["MountPac represents manufacturers of food processing, packaging, and product inspection machines -> db, /", "Headquartered in Lake Oswego, Oregon -> db", "Sales team includes Jeff Smith, Jarod Smotherman, Tyler Larson, Josh Wiechman -> /about-us", "Parts & service team includes Ann Beaudry, Kelly Roberts, Scott Thompson -> /about-us", "Provides design through install and support for machinery and automation solutions -> db, /", "Product categories: sizing/grading, de-clumpers, washing/scrubbing/peeling, sorters, conveyors, pouch filling/sealing, inspection -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "MountPac has represented industry leading manufacturers of food processing, packaging and product inspection machines for over fifty years.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mountain-pacific-machinery-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mountain States Agency LLC was founded in 2012 in the historic town of Bernalillo, New Mexico. The company operates as a manufacturer’s representative agency for electrical products, led by principals Samantha Barnes and James Ross. From its start, the firm focused on building relationships across a territory that spans New Mexico, Colorado, eastern Wyoming, El Paso, Texas, and Scottsbluff, Nebraska.

Its team of roughly a dozen professionals includes dedicated product line managers for each represented line, a vice president of operations, and inside sales and marketing staff. The company does not manufacture products itself; instead, it acts as the local sales and engineering interface for brands such as Eaton Crouse‑Hinds, EPCO, and Eaton Bussmann series.

The agency’s manufacturers specialize in areas such as energy‑efficient lighting control, surge protection, and pre‑fabricated power equipment. By aligning with these product lines, Mountain States Agency addresses needs ranging from lighting retrofits to motor starter protection across its multi‑state footprint.

The founders built the business on a philosophy of “hard work and superior customer service,” aiming to deliver value and solutions in what they describe as the most ethical manner. That relationship‑driven approach, combined with deep product knowledge, remains the core of its market position.', certifications=ARRAY['ULLISTED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Manufacturer representation for electrical products", "Product line management", "Territory sales coverage", "Technical sales support", "Marketing and administrative support"], "industries": ["Energy-efficient lighting control", "Lighting", "Electrical products"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Founded on hard work and superior customer service", "Ethical, relationship-driven representation for manufacturers and distributors", "Dedicated product line managers for each represented brand", "Multi-state territory coverage across the Mountain West"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2012 -> /", "Headquartered in Bernalillo, New Mexico -> db", "Principals: Samantha Barnes, James Ross -> /about-us", "Team includes product line managers, VP of Operations, inside sales and marketing -> /about-us", "Territories: New Mexico, Colorado, Eastern Wyoming, El Paso TX, Scottsbluff NE -> /", "Represents manufacturers such as Eaton Crouse-Hinds, EPCO, Eaton Bussmann series -> /", "Mission: bring value and solutions in ethical manner -> /", "Industries: Energy-efficient lighting control -> db", "Certification: ULLISTED -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Mountain States Agency is a Manufacturer Representative Agency for Electrical Products.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mountain-states-agency-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mountain Wire Rope Service is a family-owned business based in Selinsgrove, Pennsylvania. The company traces its roots to 1984 when Dale R. Walters, who had worked in the wire rope industry since 1968 at Paulsen Wire Rope Corp. in Sunbury, founded the firm. After Walters'' death in October 2014, his daughter Whitney Walters-Anderson and her husband JT Anderson took over ownership; both had apprenticed under Dale and each brings more than 20 years of experience as a wire rope inspector and splicer.

The company specializes in aerial ropeway wire rope, offering splicing, repairs, inspections, magnetic rope testing, and sales of wire rope and lubricants. Operating from its central Pennsylvania location, the team travels worldwide to service wire rope from Maine to Jamaica. They inspect approximately 2 million feet of wire rope annually and, on a peak winter day, have 350 million people riding on lifts serviced by Mountain Wire Rope.

The primary customers are ski areas, amusement parks, and aerial tram operators. The firm currently services 135 ski areas and 10 amusement parks and aerial trams throughout the Caribbean, providing on-site inspection, splicing, and testing services.

Mountain Wire Rope Service distinguishes itself through its deep specialization in aerial ropeway applications and its ability to deploy inspection and splicing crews globally. The business was built on Dale Walters'' decades of industry experience and continues as a family-led operation focused on wire rope safety and reliability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire rope splicing", "Wire rope repairs", "Wire rope inspections", "Magnetic rope testing", "Wire rope sales", "Wire rope lubricant sales", "Aerial ropeway wire rope services"], "industries": ["Ski areas", "Amusement parks", "Aerial trams", "Aerial ropeway"], "materials": ["Wire rope", "Wire rope lubricant"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Services 135 ski areas and 10 amusement parks/aerial trams across the Caribbean", "Inspects 2 million feet of wire rope annually", "Family-owned with second-generation leadership since 2014", "Provides magnetic rope testing and wire rope lubricant sales", "Deploys splicing and inspection crews worldwide from Maine to Jamaica"], "facts_used": ["Family-owned business founded in 1984 by Dale R. Walters -> /", "Dale Walters began career in 1968 at Paulsen Wire Rope Corp. -> /", "Whitney Walters-Anderson and JT Anderson took over in 2014 -> /", "Specializes in aerial ropeway wire rope, splicing, inspections, sales, magnetic rope testing -> /", "Services 135 ski areas, 10 amusement parks and aerial trams throughout Caribbean -> /", "Inspects 2 million feet of wire rope yearly -> /", "On busy winter day, 350 million people in air on serviced lifts -> /", "Services: Splicing, Repairs, Inspections, Magnetic Rope Testing, Wire Rope Sales, Wire Rope Lube Sales -> /services", "Headquarters: Selinsgrove, Pennsylvania -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Traveling the world to service wire rope from Maine to Jamaica, we service 135 ski areas, 10 amusement parks and aerial trams throughout the Caribbean.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mountain-wire-rope-service' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mountaineer Fabricators Inc. was founded in 1923 in Nitro, West Virginia. The company began as a family-owned operation and was purchased from the original family owners in 2004, relocating to newly constructed facilities in Nitro.

The company designs and manufactures ASME pressure vessels, pre-fabricated piping assemblies, and modular skidded process units. Its in-house shop provides plate rolling, engine lathe work, horizontal and vertical boring, CNC milling and drilling, and surface grinding. Pressure testing capabilities include hydrostatic, pneumatic, helium leak detection, and nitrogen sensitive leak services. An engineering department uses Compress® by Codeware and AutoCAD for ASME Section VIII Division 1 design calculations.

Mountaineer serves the oil and gas, power, chemical, and natural gas industries with prefabricated piping assemblies, launchers and receivers, and valve settings that reduce field construction costs. Additional markets include air separation, steam piping, oxygen and nitrogen production, food processing, Kevlar production, glass wool manufacturing, and data center infrastructure.

